  "notes": "Age is decoded from the 7-digit CP number on a separate tag/sticker, NOT from the serial number. Page states the chart is a 'guideline for approximate manufacture year' (1988 into 2023), so every band is approximate:true. Bands 1988-2008 are printed in full and are consecutive with no gaps or overlaps. Bands 2009-2022 are printed with masked xxx endings/beginnings (e.g. 6150xxx); the file expands each xxx prefix to its full 1000-number block, so every CP in a shared-prefix block falls in two bands and must decode to 'cannot determine', never first-match. 2023 device band: the chart prints 2023 as beginning 8067xxx with ending '???', so its entire known range coincides with 2022's ending block; the 8067000-8067999 band for 2023 exists ONLY to force 'cannot determine' on that block, it is not a true 2023 range, and CPs above 8067999 match zero bands (2023 continuation and 2024+ unknown from this chart). Fallback if device bands are rejected: truncate 2022 to max 8066999 and drop 2023. NORMALIZATION (resolved): locked normalization strips spaces, so the prose form 'CP 2530051' normalizes to 'CP2530051'; pattern ^CP\\d{7}$ with year positions [2,9] is therefore correct. CAVEATS: AquaBalance model CP numbers are NOT sequential and the chart may not suffice for them (serial alone cannot distinguish them); 6-digit CP numbers are generally early-1980s and prior and the page directs techs to contact Weil-McLain (pattern covers 7-digit only; zero-padded 6-digit values fall below the chart and correctly do not match). Page header misspells parent as 'Marely-Wylain'; history section spelling 'Marley-Wylain' used here. Page header lists Williamson Thermoflo as a related brand; sharing of the CP system is NOT verified, so it is not listed as a sister.",
